How to manage MOD_FEM code.

I. Writing a new module.

1. Create a new directory with the name conforming to naming conventions.

2. Place source files and internal headers files in the directory.

3. Create local Makefile in the directory of your module according to rules
	(taking any of the provided local Makefile's as an example)

3. Modify the main Makefile in src directory:

	a/ write a new option in initial message on how to perform make
	b/ define a new symbol for developed library (libraries)
	c/ create a new block for your new option 
		- compose directories in which to perform local make's
		- include your new libraries in the final linking 

4. Modify (if necessary) platform files to include new libraries, 
	perform new optimizations, etc.)
